, which is 60. This results in 2100', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 35 and 69?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's calculate the product of 35 and 69 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 35 by the ones place digit of 69 (which is 9):**.\n   \\[.\n   35 \\times 9 = 315.\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply 35 by the tens place digit of 69 (which is 60):**.\n   \\[.\n   35 \\times 60 = 2100.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Add the results of the two steps together:**.\n   \\[.\n   315 + 2100 = 2415.\n   \\].\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '2615'}
